
  Archetypes are tools meant to help with character creation. They give a rough idea of what type of character you'll end up with
by looking at your attribute distribution. It does this by classifying your character's attributes into two categories:

# Primary Attributes: Your highest attribute and the ones which are within 2 points of it.
# Secondary Attributes: Attributes which are not within 2 points of your highest one.

  Depending on the specific combination of primary attributes your character has they will gain an archetype.
These combinations are written next to their names. Each attribute also gives your character a specific attribute trait.
These can range from widely useful to highly specific but each of them provide a real, tangible benefit to your character.

  Your character's archetype might change as your character levels up and increases their attributes.
This will change your archetype trait so you ought to be careful when planning your stat increases.

List of Archetypes:

# Beefcake (MGT):
# Natural Defense: If you’re unarmored or lightly armored add your MGT modifier to your DR. When you’re heavily armored add half your MGT modifier rounded down to your DR.

# Scout (AGI):
# Sharp Reflexes: You have double-advantage on every initiative roll you make.

# Occultist (WIL):
# Natural Spellcaster: You gain an additional spell every time you gain one through level up and character creation.

# Heartbreaker (PRS):
# Charming Charisma: You have advantage on every Persuade and Deceive skill check you make.

# Veteran (MGT/AGI):
# Battle Master: Your multiple attack penalty is reduced from -5/-10 to -4/-8 but only for melee weapons.

# Spellblade (MGT/WIL):
# Weapon Conduit: You can use any weapon as your magical conduit. This weapon now deals magical damage.

# Captain (MGT/PRS):
# Team Player: When you pass your turn to a teammate during battle, they gain advantage on the next roll they make.

# Trickster (AGI/WIL):
# Quick Feet: Your movement speed is increased by 10ft and in turn your swimming and climbing speed are increased by 5ft. And the disengage action costs only 1 action point.

# Assassin (AGI/PRS):
# Backstab: Any attack roll you make that succeeds against an enemy which either hasn’t noticed you or has their back turned to you is treated as a critical hit.

# Shaman (WIL/PRS):
# Primal Form: You can transform into an animal form of your choosing from the list below with the use of an action. Detail it further

# Outlander (MGT/AGI/WIL):
# Relentless: After taking down an enemy you regain d4 + MGT points of health.

# Sharpshooter (MGT/AGI/PRS):
# Steady Aim: If you do not move in your turn on your next one you gain advantage on every ranged attack you make.

# Combatant (MGT/WIL/PRS):
# Unarmed Offense: Your unarmed strike deals d8 damage instead of 1. Your unarmed strike gains the finesse trait and it does not incur a multiple attack penalty.

# Magician (AGI/WIL/PRS):
# Calm Mind: During half-rests you additionally lose stress points equal to half your WIL modifier rounded down. During fullürests you additionally lose stress points equal to your WIL modifier.

# Jack of All Trades (WIL/AGI/WIL/PRS):
# Still Better Than Master of One: You gain a +1 to every roll you make.
